{
  "name": "How to Brighten Up a Dim Laundry Space",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Tired of squinting in your laundry room? A little light can go a long way in making this chore space much more pleasant and functional. The key is to think about layered lighting, not just one bulb. Start by assessing where your current lighting falls short—are there dark spots around the machines, or is your folding area always in shadow? Once you pinpoint those dark zones, you can start to strategically add light.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2",
      "text": "First, consider upgrading your main ceiling fixture to something brighter, like a modern LED light, especially in the 4000K-5000K range, which is great for visibility. Then, think about task lighting: under-cabinet lights can dramatically brighten your folding counter, and strip lighting above appliances can reduce shadows around them. It's really about ensuring even illumination, especially at entrances, around the washer and dryer, and along any walking paths. Remember, you want to improve visibility without causing annoying glare. If your laundry space is enclosed within cabinets, low-voltage or bulkhead-style lighting works well there. HH Remodeling LLC can help you plan and install effective lighting solutions that transform your dim laundry room into a well-lit, efficient space.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    }
  ],
  "@type": "HowTo",
